You can install Drozer (Python 3 console + Android agent APK) on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) using pipx and GitHub releases.
(Note: All URLs below are built from split variables so your browser extension never rewrites or strips the links.)

1. Install the Drozer Console via pipx

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y adb pipx python3-dev build-essential libprotobuf-dev protobuf-compiler curl && \
pipx ensurepath && \
pipx install drozer
Use code with caution.

2. Download the Matching Drozer Android Agent APK (drozer-agent.apk)

bash
mkdir -p ~/tools/drozer && cd ~/tools/drozer && \
PROTO="https" && \
API_HOST="api.github" && \
TLD="com" && \
AGENT_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/ReversecLabs/drozer-agent/releases/latest" && \
AGENT_URL=$(curl -s "$AGENT_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+\.apk' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading Agent: $AGENT_URL" && \
curl -sL "$AGENT_URL" -o drozer-agent.apk && \
ls -lh ~/tools/drozer/drozer-agent.apk
Use code with caution.

3. Verify drozer & Quick Connection Setup

bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"

which drozer && drozer --help | head -n 6
Use code with caution.
(To connect to a running Android device/emulator: install adb install ~/tools/drozer/drozer-agent.apk, turn on the Embedded Server inside the Drozer app on the phone, forward port 31415 with adb forward tcp:31415 tcp:31415, and run drozer console connect.)
